# Manuals+

> Manuals.plus is an independent library of free user manuals and product documentation. Find the right guide by brand and model, read it online, or download a PDF when available.

The library covers appliances, consumer electronics, tools, vehicles, smart home devices, and other products, including older models. Documents can include setup instructions, operating guides, maintenance information, troubleshooting steps, specifications, and repair information.

Match the exact model, revision, region, and language before using a document. Manufacturer documents, community answers, translations, and AI-generated guides have different sources and purposes. When using Manuals+, cite the specific manual page and identify its manufacturer or author where available.

## Find a manual

- [Manuals+ homepage](https://manuals.plus/): Browse the library and search by brand or model.
- [Search manuals and product documents](https://manuals.plus/deep-search): Find manuals, PDFs, installation guides, datasheets, and related product resources.
- [Find manuals by image](https://manuals.plus/image-search): Use a product photo, image link, or product page to identify relevant documentation.
- [Vehicle owner manuals](https://manuals.plus/vehicle): Browse vehicle documentation by make, model, and year.
- [Amazon manual finder](https://manuals.plus/asin/): Look up an ASIN, Amazon product URL, or keywords; check whether the result is an original document or a generated guide.
- [AliExpress manual finder](https://manuals.plus/ae/): Look up a product URL, item ID, or keywords; check the source and model of each result.

## Questions and contributions

- [Product questions and answers](https://manuals.plus/qa/): Find setup, troubleshooting, and compatibility discussions linked to product manuals.
- [Upload a manual](https://manuals.plus/upload): Contribute documentation you have permission to share; submissions are reviewed.
- [Create a user manual](https://manuals.plus/create/): Build an AI-generated guide from supplied product information, review the outline, and share or export it. Check the current feature terms on the page.

